WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
I gotta talk to the people
of America for a second

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:02.773
if it's all right.
All right.

00:00:02.773 --> 00:00:04.740
Because this is a pretty
interesting stuff.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.130
I wanna talk about here
at the top of the show.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.540
You folks may not know this

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.170
but all throughout Europe

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:11.900
there are late night talk shows

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.860
which are by and large imitations
of American talk shows.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.105
This is a sprung up in
the last couple of years-

00:00:19.105 --> 00:00:21.170
Yeah, when I've been
on vacation over there

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.610
It's amazing how close some of them are

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.390
to talk shows here.
To talk shows here.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:26.840
Yeah.
Yeah, It's pretty cool.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:31.030
Well recently, I was invited
to fly to Cologne, Germany

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:34.016
to appear on the Harald Schmidt Show.

00:00:34.016 --> 00:00:34.940
(audience laughing)

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:35.930
This is honest to God.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.030
This is true.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.720
He is known as the David
Letterman of Germany

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.270
and he borrows a lot of
stuff from David Letterman.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:46.030
And he borrowed some stuff from our show

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:47.460
which is a high compliment.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.290
And anyway, I had heard about this show

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:51.300
and when I got the invitation

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.670
I was intrigued.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:56.730
So I decided to fly to
Germany appear on the show

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.850
and see all the sights of Cologne

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.170
'cause I've never been there.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:02.960
And we of course brought a camera crew.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.540
We filmed the whole thing

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.070
and we're gonna show it to you right now

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:08.850
because it's pretty
interesting what happened.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:09.753
We hope you enjoy.

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:13.384
(bright music)

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.530
I've heard that my fans in Europe

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.400
can be a little overzealous.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:40.370
So while I'm here and NBC
has assigned me a bodyguard.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:45.370
This is Barn and he's gonna
pretty much make sure that

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.673
you know everyone keeps their distance.

00:01:50.424 --> 00:01:53.424
(audience laughing)

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:22.240
(bright music)

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.640
We're in the basement of a beer hall

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.470
and this thing is pretty interesting.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:29.010
It's designed just for
people that need to vomit.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.330
There's a handle on either side

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:35.300
and in here and there's a nice wide space

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.833
to accommodate cone vomit.

00:02:39.097 --> 00:02:41.090
(mumbles)

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.320
You vomit, you move away.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.160
These lights sensors flush the vomit

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.242
and then you go upstairs to
drink some more, (mumbles)

00:02:49.242 --> 00:02:54.078
(audience laughing and clapping)

00:02:54.078 --> 00:02:54.911
Thank you.

00:02:56.116 --> 00:02:57.150
Thank you very much.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.930
